{"type":"message","id":"d5584070","parentId":"f3281c72","timestamp":"2026-05-19T08:06:19.556Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The POST request keeps failing with 1101. Let me try a simpler approach to see if it's the format or the endpoint.Actually wait - I notice the error code 1101 is a Cloudflare Workers error. The error message says \"Worker threw an unhandled exception\". This could mean:\n1. The /send endpoint requires a different request format\n2. The endpoint might not exist or the worker crashed\n3. The API key might be invalid for POST requests\n\nLet me try without the Content-Type header, or try with a very simple message.\n\nActually wait, looking at the error message carefully - it says \"error code: 1101\" which is what Cloudflare Workers returns when there's an unhandled exception in the worker script itself. \n\nThis suggests the worker might have crashed when processing my request, so let me try scaling back the message complexity to see if that helps.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-198e38fc-9f53-4492-a1cb-21a793b1364d","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat test 08:01 UTC\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":20107,"output":278,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20497,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779177946415,"responseId":"chatcmpl-3694709c-25d4-4370-9325-540af2e44e58"}}
